During the transition period, the transitional adjustment amount will be partially included in (ie
added back to) Common Equity Tier 1 capital. A fraction of the transitional adjustment amount
(based on the number of years in the transition period) will be included in Common Equity Tier
1 capital during the first year of the transition period, with the proportion included in Common
Equity Tier 1 capital phased out each year thereafter during the course of the transition period
on a straight line basis. The impact of ECL provisions on Common Equity Tier 1 capital must not
be fully neutralised during the transition period.
90.15
The transitional adjustment amount included in Common Equity Tier 1 capital each year during
the transition period must be taken through to other measures of capital as appropriate (eg
Tier 1 capital and total capital), and hence to the calculation of the leverage ratio and of large
exposures limits.
90.16
Jurisdictions must choose between applying the consequential adjustments listed below or a
simpler approach to ensure that banks do not receive inappropriate capital relief. (An example
of a simpler approach that would not provide inappropriate capital relief would be amortising
the transitional arrangement more rapidly than otherwise.)
Account should be taken of tax eﬀects in calculating the impact of ECL accounting on
1.
