For the purposes of calculating capital requirements, a Multilateral Development Bank (MDB) is
an institution created by a group of countries that provides financing and professional advice
for economic and social development projects. MDBs have large sovereign memberships and
may include both developed and/or developing countries. Each MDB has its own independent
legal and operational status, but with a similar mandate and a considerable number of joint
owners.","Basel Framework, CRE20, num. 20.13, p. 184","pymupdf+bookmark_title_match+numeral_split","0.99","false",""
