20.69
Real estate is immovable property that is land, including agricultural land and forest, or
anything treated as attached to land, in particular buildings, in contrast to being treated as
movable/personal property. The real estate exposure asset class consists of:
Exposures secured by real estate that are classified as “regulatory real estate”
1.
exposures.
Exposures secured by real estate that are classified as “other real estate” exposures.
2.
Exposures that are classified as “land acquisition, development and construction” (ADC)
3.
exposures.","Basel Framework, CRE20, num. 20.66-20.69, pp. 201-202","pymupdf+bookmark_title_match+numeral_split","0.99","false",""
