22.51
In paragraphs CRE22.49 to CRE22.50:
“Sovereigns” includes: PSEs that are treated as sovereigns by the national supervisor, as
1.
well as multilateral development banks receiving a 0% risk weight.
“Other issuers” includes: PSEs that are not treated as sovereigns by the national
2.
supervisor.
“Securitisation exposures” refers to exposures that meet the definition set forth in the
3.
securitisation framework.
“Cash in the same currency” refers to eligible cash collateral specified in CRE22.34(1).
4.
22.52
The haircut for currency risk (Hfx) where exposure and collateral are denominated in diﬀerent
currencies is 8% (also based on a 10-business day holding period and daily mark-to-market).
22.53
