The comprehensive approach: adjustment for diﬀerent holding periods and non-daily mark-to-
market or remargining
22.56
For some transactions, depending on the nature and frequency of the revaluation and
remargining provisions, diﬀerent holding periods and thus diﬀerent haircuts must be applied.
The framework for collateral haircuts distinguishes between repo-style transactions (ie
repo/reverse repos and securities lending/borrowing), ”other capital markets-driven
transactions” (ie OTC derivatives transactions and margin lending) and secured lending. In
capital-market-driven transactions and repo-style transactions, the documentation contains
remargining clauses; in secured lending transactions, it generally does not.
22.57
