On-balance sheet netting
22.68
A bank may use the net exposure of loans and deposits as the basis for its capital adequacy
calculation in accordance with the formula in CRE22.46, when the bank:
has a well-founded legal basis for concluding that the netting or oﬀsetting agreement is
1.
enforceable in each relevant jurisdiction regardless of whether the counterparty is
insolvent or bankrupt;
is able at any time to determine those assets and liabilities with the same counterparty
2.
