4.
22.69
When calculating the net exposure described in the paragraph above, assets (loans) are
treated as exposure and liabilities (deposits) as collateral. The haircuts are zero except when a
currency mismatch exists. A 10-business day holding period applies when daily mark-to-market
is conducted. For on-balance sheet netting, the requirements in CRE22.49 and CRE22.59 and
CRE22.10 to CRE22.14 must be applied.
Guarantees and credit derivatives
Operational requirements for guarantees and credit derivatives
