The add-on for the commodity derivative asset class (AddOnCommodity) within a netting set is
calculated using the following steps:
Step 1: Calculate the eﬀective notional for each trade in the netting set that is in the
1.
commodity derivative asset class. This is calculated as the product of the following three
terms: (i) the adjusted notional of the trade (d); (ii) the supervisory delta adjustment of
the trade (δ); and (iii) the maturity factor (MF). That is, for each trade i, the eﬀective
notional Di is calculated as Di = di * MFi * δi, where each term is as defined in CRE52.33 to
CRE52.53.
Step 2: Allocate the trades in commodity derivative asset class to hedging sets. In the
2.
commodity derivative asset class there are four hedging sets consisting of derivatives
