Cash-collateralised securities lending transactions are exempted from the haircut floors where:
Securities are lent (to the bank) at long maturities and the lender of securities reinvests
1.
or employs the cash at the same or shorter maturity, therefore not giving rise to material
maturity or liquidity mismatch.
Securities are lent (to the bank) at call or at short maturities, giving rise to liquidity risk,
2.
only if the lender of the securities reinvests the cash collateral into a reinvestment fund
or account subject to regulations or regulatory guidance meeting the minimum standards
for reinvestment of cash collateral by securities lenders set out in Section 3.1 of the
Policy Framework for Addressing Shadow Banking Risks in Securities Lending and
Repos.
247 For this purpose, banks may rely on representations by securities lenders that
their reinvestment of cash collateral meets the minimum standards.
