denominated and (ii) the following tenors: 0.25 years, 0.5 years, 1 year, 2 years, 3 years,
5 years, 10 years, 15 years, 20 years and 30 years, to which delta risk factors are
assigned.
274
The risk-free yield curve per currency should be constructed using money market
1.
instruments held in the trading book that have the lowest credit risk, such as
overnight index swaps (OIS). Alternatively, the risk-free yield curve should be
based on one or more market-implied swap curves used by the bank to mark
positions to market. For example, interbank oﬀered rate (BOR) swap curves.
