Commodity risk factors
Delta commodity: the commodity delta risk factors are all the commodity spot prices.
1.
However for some commodities such as electricity (which is defined to fall within bucket
3 (energy – electricity and carbon trading) in MAR21.82 the relevant risk factor can either
be the spot or the forward price, as transactions relating to commodities such as
electricity are more frequent on the forward price than transactions on the spot price.
Commodity delta risk factors are defined along two dimensions:
legal terms with respect to the delivery location
277 of the commodity; and
1.
time to maturity of the traded instrument at the following tenors: 0 years, 0.25
2.
