FAQ1
MAR21.68 includes , which equals 1 where the two sensitivities within the same
bucket are related to the same securitisation tranche, or 40% otherwise. There is
no issuer factor. Does this mean that two sensitivities relating to the same issuer
but diﬀerent tranches require 40% correlation?
Yes. There is no granularity for issuers in the delta CSR securitisation part as set
out in MAR21.10. Where two tranches have exactly the same issuer, same tenor
and same basis, but diﬀerent tranches (ie diﬀerent credit quality), the correlation
must be 40%.
