FAQ1
For instruments with commodity spreads as underlying, are the spreads considered
a risk factor, or does the instrument have to be decomposed? For example, if there
is a swap on the spread between WTI and Brent, will delta on the spread be
reported, or will delta of WTI and delta of Brent be reported individually?
Instruments with a spread as their underlying are considered sensitive to diﬀerent
risk factors. In the example cited, the swap will be sensitive to both WTI and Brent,
each of which require a capital charge at the risk factor level (ie delta of WTI and
delta of Brent). The correlation to aggregate capital charges is specified in
