The ES for market risk capital purposes is therefore expressed as follows, where:
The ES for the portfolio using the above reduced set of risk factors (ESR,S), is calculated
1.
based on the most severe 12-month period of stress available over the observation
horizon.
ESR,S is then scaled up by the ratio of (i) the current ES using the full set of risk factors to
2.
