Calculation of default risk capital requirement
33.18
Banks must have a separate internal model to measure the default risk of trading book
positions. The general criteria in MAR30.1 to MAR30.4 and the qualitative standards in
MAR30.5 to MAR30.16 also apply to the default risk model.
33.19
Default risk is the risk of direct loss due to an obligor’s default as well as the potential for
indirect losses that may arise from a default event.","Basel Framework, MAR33, num. 33.17-33.19, p. 678","pymupdf+bookmark_title_match+numeral_split","0.99","false",""
