In addition, opposite positions in the same category of instruments
322 can in certain
circumstances be regarded as matched and allowed to oﬀset fully. To qualify for this
treatment, the positions must relate to the same underlying instruments, be of the same
nominal value and be denominated in the same currency.
323 In addition:
for futures: oﬀsetting positions in the notional or underlying instruments to which the
1.
futures contract relates must be for identical products and mature within seven days of
each other;
for swaps and FRAs: the reference rate (for floating rate positions) must be identical and
2.
the coupon closely matched (ie within 15 basis points); and
