Banks that write options will be allowed to include delta-weighted options positions within the
simplified standardised approach set out in MAR40.3 to MAR40.73. Such options should be
reported as a position equal to the market value of the underlying multiplied by the delta.
However, since delta does not suﬃciently cover the risks associated with options positions,
banks will also be required to measure gamma (which measures the rate of change of delta)
and vega (which measures the sensitivity of the value of an option with respect to a change in
volatility) sensitivities in order to calculate the total capital requirement. These sensitivities will
be calculated according to an approved exchange model or to the bank’s proprietary options
pricing model subject to oversight by the national authority.
347
