1.
in exactly the same way as for the reduced version calculation of the BA-CVA.
SNHC is a quantity that gives recognition to the reduction in CVA risk of the counterparty
2.
c arising from the bank’s use of single-name hedges of credit spread risk. See MAR50.23
for its calculation.
IH is a quantity that gives recognition to the reduction in CVA risk across all
3.
counterparties arising from the bank’s use of index hedges. See MAR50.24 for its
