of 250 independent observations under several assumptions about the actual percentage of
outcomes that the model captures (ie these are binomial probabilities). For example, the left-
hand portion of Table 1 sets out probabilities associated with an accurate model (that is, a true
coverage level of 99%). Under these assumptions, the column labelled “exact” reports that
exactly five exceptions can be expected in 6.7% of the samples.
