"c_8a5de5a0c560c9b5","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026","Basel Framework","Basel III - Basel Framework consolidado","BCBS/BIS","INT","international_standard","in_force","","2026-01-01","","https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/basel-framework.pdf","fuentes_descargadas/02_normativa_internacional/18_bis_basel_framework_2026.pdf","acf3759fc231fb8f13131e50b12ad11e18bc9ebe53f105595fd8e16609a3547f","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026#nsec-90-occ5","90","numbered_section","LEV Leverage ratio > 90 Transition","814","815","LEV90
Transition
This chapter describes transitional
arrangements that apply to the leverage ratio
buﬀer requirement for global systemically
important banks.
Version eﬀective as of 01
January 2023
First version in the format of the consolidated
framework. Sets out the transitional
arrangements for the G-SIB leverage ratio
buﬀer introduced in the December 2017 Basel
III publication and the revised implementation
date announced on 27 March 2020.
90.1
The leverage ratio buﬀer requirement on 1 January 2023 shall be based on the Financial
Stability Board's 2021 list of global systemically important banks (G-SIBs), based on end-2020
data. For banks that are subsequently identified as G-SIBs or which are no longer identified as
G-SIBs, the same transitional arrangements will apply as in the higher loss-absorbency
requirement framework.
90.2
The leverage ratio buﬀer requirement will be updated annually to reflect the annual updated
list of G-SIB requirements. G-SIBs subject to a revised higher loss-absorbency requirement
would also be subject to a revised leverage ratio buﬀer requirement, calibrated at 50% of the
former requirement. Both requirements would follow the same implementation arrangements.
Jurisdictions may impose a higher leverage ratio buﬀer requirement.","Basel Framework, LEV90, pp. 814-815","pymupdf+bookmark_title_match","0.99","false",""
