With the adoption of Option 3, the increase in holdings of Level 2A assets within the banking
sector (to substitute for Level 1 assets which are of higher quality but in shortage) may give
rise to additional price and market liquidity risks, especially in times of stress when
concentrated asset holdings have to be liquidated. In order to mitigate this risk, the jurisdiction
intending to adopt Option 3 should ensure that only Level 2A assets that are of comparable
quality to Level 1 assets in the domestic currency are allowed to be used under this option (ie
to exceed the 40% cap). Level 2B assets must remain subject to the 15% cap. The jurisdiction
should demonstrate how this can be achieved in its supervisory framework, having regard to
the following aspects:
The adoption of higher qualifying standards for additional Level 2A assets: apart from
1.
