"c_7f0b57a18a5cfc67","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026","Basel Framework","Basel III - Basel Framework consolidado","BCBS/BIS","INT","international_standard","in_force","","2026-01-01","","https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/basel-framework.pdf","fuentes_descargadas/02_normativa_internacional/18_bis_basel_framework_2026.pdf","acf3759fc231fb8f13131e50b12ad11e18bc9ebe53f105595fd8e16609a3547f","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026#nsec-25-occ3","25","numbered_section","DIS Disclosure requirements > 25 Composition of capital and TLAC > num. 25.5","1162","1162","Purpose: Provide a description of the main features of a bank's regulatory capital
instruments and other TLAC-eligible instruments, as applicable, that are recognised as part of
its capital base / TLAC resources.
Scope of application: The template is mandatory for all banks. In addition to completing
the template for all regulatory capital instruments, G-SIB resolution entities should complete
the template (including lines 3a and 34a) for all other TLAC-eligible instruments that are
recognised as external TLAC resources by the resolution entities, starting from the TLAC
conformance date. Internal TLAC instruments and other senior debt instruments are not
covered in this template.
Content: Quantitative and qualitative information as required.
Frequency: Table CCA should be posted on a bank's website. It should be updated whenever
the bank issues or repays a capital instrument (or other TLAC-eligible instrument where
applicable), and whenever there is a redemption, conversion/writedown or other material
change in the nature of an existing instrument. Updates should, at a minimum, be made
semiannually. Banks should include the web link in each Pillar 3 report to the issuances made
over the previous period.
Format: Flexible.
Accompanying information: Banks are required to make available on their websites the
full terms and conditions of all instruments included in regulatory capital and TLAC.
