Definitions
Defaulted exposure: such exposures must be reported net of write-oﬀs and gross of (ie
ignoring) allowances/impairments. For a bank using the standardised approach for credit
risk, the default exposures in Templates CR1 and CR2 should correspond to exposures
that are ""past due for more than 90 days"", as stated in CRE20.104.
Loans and debt securities that have defaulted since the last reporting period: refers to
any loan or debt securities that became marked as defaulted during the reporting period.
Return to non-defaulted status: refers to loans or debt securities that returned to non-
default status during the reporting period.
Amounts written oﬀ: both total and partial write-oﬀs.
Other changes: balancing items that are necessary to enable total to reconcile.
