When the accounting framework is IFRS 9, “impaired exposures” are those that
are considered “credit-impaired” in the meaning of IFRS 9 Appendix A. When
the accounting framework is US GAAP, “impaired exposures” are those
exposures for which credit losses are measured under ASC Topic 326 and for
which the bank has recorded a partial write-oﬀ/writedown.
