Counterparty credit risk
This chapter describes counterparty credit risk
and credit valuation adjustment disclosure
requirements.
Version eﬀective as of 01
January 2023
Removes the CVA template (CCR2), which is
now specified in a separate chapter (DIS51).
Updated to take account of new
implementation date as announced on 27
March 2020.
Introduction
42.1
DIS42 includes all exposures in the banking book and trading book that are subject to a
counterparty credit risk charge, including the charges applied to exposures to central
counterparties (CCPs).
