"c_ba0dabc0f5032b1c","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026","Basel Framework","Basel III - Basel Framework consolidado","BCBS/BIS","INT","international_standard","in_force","","2026-01-01","","https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/basel-framework.pdf","fuentes_descargadas/02_normativa_internacional/18_bis_basel_framework_2026.pdf","acf3759fc231fb8f13131e50b12ad11e18bc9ebe53f105595fd8e16609a3547f","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026#nsec-60-occ3","60","numbered_section","DIS Disclosure requirements > 60 Operational risk > num. 60.1","1291","1291","60.1
The disclosure requirements under this section are:
Table ORA – General qualitative information on a bank’s operational risk framework
1.
Template OR1 – Historical losses
2.
Template OR2 – Business indicator and subcomponents
3.
Template OR3 – Minimum required operational risk capital
4.
Table ORA: General qualitative information on a bank's operational risk framework
TABLE.1
Purpose: To describe the main characteristics and elements of a bank's operational risk
management framework.
Scope of application: The table is mandatory for all banks.
Content: Qualitative information.
Frequency: Annual.
Format: Flexible.
Banks must describe:
(a) Their policies, frameworks and guidelines for the management of operational risk.
(b) The structure and organisation of their operational risk management and control
function.
(c) Their operational risk measurement system (ie the systems and data used to
measure operational risk in order to estimate the operational risk capital charge).
(d) The scope and main context of their reporting framework on operational risk to
executive management and to the board of directors.
(e) The risk mitigation and risk transfer used in the management of operational risk. This
includes mitigation by policy (such as the policies on risk culture, risk appetite, and
outsourcing), by divesting from high-risk businesses, and by the establishment of
controls. The remaining exposure can then be absorbed by the bank or transferred. For
instance, the impact of operational losses can be mitigated with insurance.
Template OR1: Historical losses
