"c_5e7e5480eba79117","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026","Basel Framework","Basel III - Basel Framework consolidado","BCBS/BIS","INT","international_standard","in_force","","2026-01-01","","https://www.bis.org/committees/bcbs/basel-framework/basel-framework.pdf","fuentes_descargadas/02_normativa_internacional/18_bis_basel_framework_2026.pdf","acf3759fc231fb8f13131e50b12ad11e18bc9ebe53f105595fd8e16609a3547f","int-bcbs-basel-framework-2026#nsec-60-occ3","60","numbered_section","DIS Disclosure requirements > 60 Operational risk > num. 60.1","1292","1293","Purpose: To disclose aggregate operational losses incurred over the past 10 years,
based on the accounting date of the incurred losses. This disclosure informs the
operational risk capital calculation. The general principle on retrospective disclosure set
out in DIS10.6 does not apply for this template. From the implementation date of the
template onwards, disclosure of all prior periods is required, unless firms have been
permitted by their supervisor to use fewer years in their capital calculation on a
transitional basis.
Scope of application: The table is mandatory for: (i) all banks that are in the second or
third business indicator (BI) bucket, regardless of whether their supervisor has exercised
the national discretion to set the internal loss multiplier (ILM) equal to one; and (ii) all
banks in the first BI bucket which have received supervisory approval to include internal
loss data to calculate their operational risk capital requirements.
Content: Quantitative information.
Frequency: Annual.
Format: Fixed. National supervisors may prescribe further guidance regarding the
disclosure of the total number of exclusions in rows 4 and 9.
Accompanying narrative: Banks are expected to supplement the template with
narrative commentary explaining the rationale in aggregate, for new loss exclusions since
the previous disclosure. Banks should disclose any other material information, in
aggregate, that would help inform users as to its historical losses or its recoveries, with
the exception of confidential and proprietary information, including information about
legal reserves.
