Principle 8:
630 An eﬀective system of banking supervision requires the supervisor to develop
and maintain a forward-looking assessment of the risk profile of individual banks, proportionate
to their systemic importance; identify, assess and address risks emanating from banks and the
banking system as a whole; have a framework in place for early intervention; and have plans in
place, in partnership with other relevant authorities, to take action to resolve banks in an
orderly manner if they become non-viable.
